---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Support"
  description="How to get help with MCP Tool Shop projects: issues, discussions, security reporting, and what to include in a report."
  currentPath="/support/"
>
  <div class="page-content">
    <h1>Support</h1>
    <p>
      Every project is maintained in the
      <a href="https://github.com/mcp-tool-shop-org" rel="noopener">mcp-tool-shop-org</a>
      GitHub organization. Issues on the relevant repository are the primary support channel,
      and every repository accepts them.
    </p>

    <h2>Reporting a bug</h2>
    <p>Open an issue on the repository for the tool. Reports that include the following get resolved fastest:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>What you expected</strong> to happen.</li>
      <li><strong>What actually happened</strong>, including the full error message.</li>
      <li><strong>Steps to reproduce</strong> the problem, or the exact command you ran.</li>
      <li><strong>Environment:</strong> operating system, runtime version (Python, Node, or .NET), and the tool version.</li>
      <li><strong>Logs</strong>, with any secrets redacted.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Most tools print a structured error with a code and a hint. Include that code in the issue title.
    </p>

    <h2>Feature requests</h2>
    <p>
      Open an issue with the <code>enhancement</code> label. Describe the use case rather than only
      the proposed solution; knowing why you need something helps us design the right thing.
    </p>

    <h2>Security</h2>
    <p>
      If you find a security vulnerability, <strong>do not open a public issue</strong>. Use
      GitHub's private vulnerability reporting on the affected repository. The organization-wide
      policy is in
      <a href="https://github.com/mcp-tool-shop-org/.github/blob/main/SECURITY.md" rel="noopener">SECURITY.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>
      For usage questions and ideas that are not bug reports, start a thread in
      <a href="https://github.com/orgs/mcp-tool-shop-org/discussions" rel="noopener">GitHub Discussions</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Response expectations</h2>
    <p>
      This is a small open-source studio. We read every issue, and clear, reproducible reports are
      handled first. There is no paid support tier and no service-level agreement.
    </p>

    <h2>Problems with this site</h2>
    <p>
      Broken links, stale catalog data, or incorrect install commands belong in the
      <a href="https://github.com/mcp-tool-shop/mcp-tool-shop/issues" rel="noopener">site repository's issues</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
